<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Maccabees</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Maccabees were the priestly family of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mattathias">Mattathias</a> and his five sons, among them <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/judas-maccabeus">Judas Maccabeus</a>, Jonathan and Simon, who led the Jewish revolt against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seleucid-empire">Seleucid Empire</a> from 167 BCE. The name comes from Judas's epithet 'Maccabeus' and is often applied to the whole family. Their victories led to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hasmonean-dynasty">Hasmonean dynasty</a>, which ruled an independent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/judaea">Judaea</a> until the Roman conquest.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/maccabees.jpg" alt="Maccabees" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: DEGA MD · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hasmonean_dynasty_family_tree.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
